# Chapter 33: Multi-Target Cross-Compilation & Hardware Backends

Cluster compiles directly to native standalone machine code across a matrix of 10 primary targets without requiring separate cross-compiler toolchains installed.

## 1. Supported Targets Matrix

View the complete target matrix:
```bash
cl targets
```

Supported triples:
- `x86_64-linux-gnu`: Tier 1 Native Host Linux (ELF 64-bit)
- `aarch64-linux-gnu`: Tier 2 ARM64 Linux (AWS Graviton, Raspberry Pi)
- `arm64-apple-darwin`: Tier 2 Apple Silicon macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4)
- `x86_64-apple-darwin`: Tier 2 Intel macOS
- `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`: Tier 1 Windows PE/COFF Native
- `wasm32-wasi`: Tier 1 Standalone WebAssembly (Cloudflare Workers, Fastly)
- `wasm32-unknown-unknown`: Tier 2 In-Browser WebAssembly
- `riscv64-linux-gnu`: Tier 2 RISC-V 64-bit hardware
- `arm-none-eabi`: Tier 2 Bare-metal embedded microcontrollers (Cortex-M)

## 2. Cross-Compiling

Compile directly by specifying the `--target` flag:
```bash
# Compile to WebAssembly
cl build src/main.cl --target wasm32-wasi -o app.wasm

# Maximum release optimizations with Link-Time Optimization and stripping
cl build src/main.cl -O3 --lto --strip -o app
```
